      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Mistakes in Date Countdown Calculations</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Timezone Midnight Discrepancies:</strong> If a calculator uses UTC midnight while your browser is in UTC-5 (EST), it may return an answer that is 1 day off. Our tool normalizes calculations to local midnight.</li>
        <li><strong>Inclusive vs. Exclusive End Dates:</strong> A countdown to tomorrow is 1 day away. But if you are counting days you will spend somewhere including both the first and last day, you need inclusive day counting. For that, use our <a href="/tools/date-difference-calculator/">Date Difference Calculator</a> which has an inclusive counting toggle.</li>
        <li><strong>Confusing Calendar Days with Business Days:</strong> 10 calendar days usually include 2 to 4 weekend days. If you need working business days excluding weekends, use our <a href="/tools/date-difference-calculator/">Date Difference Calculator</a>.</li>
